NAME
       showmount - list the exports of an NFS server

SYNOPSIS
       showmount [-e] [-a] [-d] [HOST]

DESCRIPTION
       showmount asks an NFS server (HOST, or this machine) what it shares.
       With -e it prints each exported directory and the clients allowed to
       mount it. It is the first thing to try before mounting an export or
       setting up autofs. It needs the nfs-utils package and talks to the
       server's rpcbind and mountd, so a firewall on the server must allow
       them.

OPTIONS
       -e, --exports
              List the server's exports.

       -a, --all
              List clients and the directories they have mounted.

       -d, --directories
              List only the directories clients have mounted.

EXAMPLES
           showmount -e utility.lab.example.com

SEE ALSO
       mount.nfs(8), exportfs(8), nfsstat(8)
